===SQL===
Usage: hops sql [OPTIONS] [SQL]

  Run an ad-hoc SQL query.

  Provide the SQL as a positional argument, or use ``-f`` to read from a file,
  or ``-i`` to read from stdin (useful in shell pipelines).

  Args:     ctx: Click context.     sql: SQL string passed positionally.
  sql_file: Path to a file containing SQL.     from_stdin: Read SQL from
  standard input.     catalog: Trino catalog override.     schema: Trino
  schema override.     limit: Soft cap on rows printed.

Options:
  -f, --file FILE         Read SQL from a file.
  -i, --stdin             Read SQL from standard input.
  --catalog TEXT          Trino catalog (default: iceberg).
  --schema TEXT           Trino schema (default: project name lowercased).
  --limit INTEGER         Soft cap on rows printed; 0 means unlimited.
                          [default: 10000]
  --json                  Output as JSON (machine-readable; for LLMs and
                          scripts).
  -q, --quiet             Suppress success/info/warn lines; print only data +
                          errors.
  --verify / --no-verify  Verify the Hopsworks TLS certificate; --no-verify
                          skips verification for self-signed / IP-SAN-
                          mismatched certs.
  -h, --help              Show this message and exit.
